    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0260" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1293.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires at
                            London to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-12T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1913—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Aide mémoire presented today. I venture to say that the Foreign Office seems
                    entirely inclined to your views towards settling representation on the loan in
                    any of the ways suggested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
